After ascending a valk, I decided I'd like to ascend a wizard. After a number
of pre-quest deaths, I finally made it.

The early game was pretty plain. Got a BoH from perspire's ghost (played on
nethack.alt.org), which was good because Sokoban had "AoR and the only other
BoH I found all game was deep in Gehennon. It took a while to get a pet to
shopkeeper-killing status, although I got a magic whistle fairly early on
which was nice.

Some time after the quest I decided I'd go for genoless wishless, because it
didn't seem all that bad. The first interesting moment came when I was
enchanting some armor, and I was taking off my SDSM (which I got from a SD
earlier). A purple L appeared next to me. Seems it takes at least 3 turns to
take off armor, and in those 3 turns monsters were summoned, including a mmf.
My greased helm did OK, but they all got me down from 150hp to 50hp and a
little bit of brain sucking before I got control again. Teleported away and dug
down to heal. Wearing all my armor taking them on wasn't too bad. Magic
missile rocks.

Did Medusa and the castle. I think I went into Gehennon with AC -23 or so. I
didn't find much enchant armor and polying wasn't doing much for me either.
Gehennon was pretty straightforward, although searching for Vlad was a pain.
Found a couple of more toys. Had AC -27 or so when I killed Rodney and went to
the Sanctum. The Sanctum was quite exciting. Killed an arch lich after some
trouble. Hacked my way about halfway through to have another one show up. Made
my way through to the temple, where Rodney was duking it out with the priest.
He double troubled, I went in there and was beaten to a lot of hurt by the
priest, Rodneys, and the arch lich (mostly through summoning). In one turn
they took me down from 100hp to 40hp or so, when I realized I was quite poorly
prepared, not having any potions of foo healing. After some discussion
(sitting on IRC while people can watch your game and chat about it is cool),
it was decided to take off the Eye and put on the "AoLS I had in my main
inventory. It all worked out. After putting the "AoLS on I had 1 HP left.

I quickly died and resurrected, of course. At that point Rodney stole the Eye
and I was pretty low on Pw anyway. The arch lich was killed by a black dragon
(go conflict). One of the Rodneys fell to a wand of death, after which he
double troubled again. I spent my time beating on the priest/Rodney, reserving
precious magic missile for when slimes/flayers were summoned. I think one of
the Rodneys went down by whacking him. That's definitely how the priest died.
Another arch-lich came from somewhere, and must've killed Rodney near the up
stair since that's where I found another corpse. The amulet was nowhere to be
seen, so I figured it was by the upstair. It wasn't there either.

Went up to heal and regain Pw before going down again to search for it. The
arch-lich came with, and summoned Yeenoghu who was more annoying than
dangerous. Killed them both and went down. Spent some time looking for the
amulet but couldn't find it. Turned out it was at the upstair of the VS level.
I guess liches grab it as well.

Started going up. The mysterious force pulled me back 4 or 5 times. Rodney
showed up once or twice more. At my level 8 stash I used my last poly charge
to hopefully get some more EA. I think I got two more. At that point my AC was
-31, or maybe -29. Ran up to the planes. Prayed twice but didn't get crowned
(so no FoD). The planes were pretty straightforward. I had 3 cursed scrolls of
gold detection, and one orb (0:2).

Arrived on Astral and got my angel. Decided to go up the middle, pestilence.
Pestilence is pretty wimpy hp-wise but has a brutal melee attack. Killed him
pretty easily the first time, although did use a potion of full healing
afterwards. Found another scroll of EA. After verifying it wasn't cursed, I
read it for more AC. Woops, vaporized my +4 speed boots. Bravely journeyed on,
taking out any priest that came with MM range, and any angel that came by the
doorway. Meanwhile my angel was doing a stellar job killing all the insects
that were blocking Pestilence's way to me. Killed Pestilence once more. The
next time Pestilence woke up I wasn't thinking enough. Some guy with Vorpal
Blade came up and landed some hits before I teleported him away. I ended up
with 14(392) hp, ac -27, Ill and Stunned. Pestilence right next to me with (I
guess) 18 or so HP left, and surrounded by ants and my friendly angel. After
some more IRC discussion, we decided to break a wand of MM (0:7).

It worked.

Quickly took my other AoLS out of my bag and put it on. (I was wearing magical
breathing, from water.) Quaffed some healing. Decided to hell with the conduct
and grabbed one of my WoW (0:3). Wished for +3 speed boots (got +0), and a +2
shirt (got +2). My AC still sucked, but at least I was very fast again.
Continued killing priests and angels, and ventured through the door a bit.
When Pestilence woke up again and followed me in I killed him before he got
close enough.

Ran up the middle and it was the right altar. I considered wishing for some
extra style points, but figured I'd already cheated death twice so I offered
the amulet.

For actual style points I brought up the ingredients for a white russian:
ice cubes (wand of cold)
1 part vodka (cursed clear potion, unholy water)
1 part kahlua (cursed brown potion, gain ability)
1-2 parts cream (milky potion, invisibility)
Of course I'm out of RL milky potions, so no celebration drink for me.

